schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Group-size-to-governance-model comparison table
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    The article's comparison table maps group size to model: Collective
    fits 5-10 people (no legal protection, no setup effort, slow decisions);
    Working Groups fit 10-30 (low setup, medium speed); Council fits
    20-50+ (medium/high formality, fast decisions); Cooperative fits 15+
    (high formality, high setup effort, legal protection, medium decision
    speed).
  evidence: >-
    Presented as the article's own synthesized guidance table, not
    attributed to a study, survey, or dataset of actual ReFi/DAO nodes —
    the ReFi DAO Steward Council and Network Initiatives examples support
    the qualitative descriptions but not the specific numeric size bands.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/local-node-model.md
  interpretation: >-
    A practitioner heuristic useful for a rough first cut at "which model
    fits us," but the size bands overlap (e.g. Cooperative "15+" overlaps
    Working Groups "10-30" and Council "20-50+") and are not derived from
    a cited comparative study of local-node governance transitions.
  uncertainty: >-
    High for the precise numeric bands (authorial heuristic, overlapping
    ranges); low for the qualitative ordering (Collective → Working Groups →
    Council → Cooperative as increasing formality), which is well-reasoned
    within the article.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/local-node-model.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
